EFG 2 R "Wilson (1992), Figure 14" { "Player 1" "Player 2" }
"A modification of the game Do The Right Thing in which Player 2 has four strategies in the simultaneous-move game. The first equilibrium component is dual simply stable, but only because a region of dual perturbations is covered by equilibria that use the unperturbed strategies e and h; with those strategies deleted the game resembles the original, in which the first component is not dual simply stable.

Player 1 chooses a or continue; Player 2 then chooses d or continue; then Player 1 (b or c) and Player 2 (e, f, g or h) move simultaneously. The paper leaves the continuing moves unlabeled; they are called continue here."

